    For Example:

    moveOneBall(Arrays.asList(3, 4, 5, 1, 2))==>true
    Explanation: By performin 2 right shift operations, non-decreasing order can
                 be achieved for the given array.
    moveOneBall(Arrays.asList(3, 5, 4, 1, 2))==>False
    Explanation:It is not possible to get non-decreasing order for the given
                array by performing any number of right shift operations.
     */
    public boolean moveOneBall(List<Integer> arr) {

        if (arr.isEmpty()) {
            return true;
        }

        int N = arr.size();

        // find the index of the minimum element
        int minIndex = arr.indexOf(Collections.min(arr));

        // split the list into two parts at the index of the minimum element
        List<Integer> part1 = arr.subList(minIndex, N);
        List<Integer> part2 = arr.subList(0, minIndex);

        // merge the two parts in reverse order
        List<Integer> mergedList = new ArrayList<>(part2);
        mergedList.addAll(part1);

        // check if the merged list is sorted
        for (int i = 1; i < mergedList.size(); i++) {
            if (mergedList.get(i - 1) > mergedList.get(i)) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;

